# xdotool 3.20160805.1 (Ubuntu's) `mousemove 100 200 click 1`,
# byte for byte: recon/wire/trace2.log, connection 2, 24 requests.
# The 3.x generation moves the pointer with core WarpPointer and reads
# it with QueryPointer; the 4.x the tree pins moves with
# FakeInput MotionNotify [recon/wire.md 5.3]. Both have to work.
# The FakeInput pads carry `6400 c800` at 24..27 -- the WarpPointer's
# own dst_x/dst_y, left in Xlib's output buffer.
